		<Placemark id="040E9977C63FCC60F669">
			<name>Bayernoil Refinery – Neustadt/Vohburg</name>
			<description>Refinery: Bayernoil Refinery – Neustadt/Vohburg
Classification: Large refinery — not a mega-refinery
Location: Neustadt an der Donau and Vohburg, Bavaria, Germany
Owner: Joint venture;VAROPreem 51.43% (majority shareholder and operator-side lead; VARO also acquired BP&apos;s polymer-modified bitumen plant at Vohburg and BP&apos;s 9% stake in the TAL pipeline in the same deal), Rosneft Deutschland 28.57% (under German federal trusteeship via the Federal Network Agency since September 2022), Eni 20%
Capacity: Up to 10 million tonnes per year, equivalent to roughly 200,000–210,000 b/d for the two-site refinery system
Main feedstocks: Imported crude delivered through the Transalpine Pipeline system and regional pipeline connections
Main products: Gasoline, diesel, heating oil, jet fuel components, LPG and bitumen
Markets: Supplies roughly half of Bavaria&apos;s fuel demand plus northern Austria; jet fuel to Munich airport
Recent data: Explosion and fire at Vohburg site in 2018 (ten injured), activity restarted in 2020 + Fire occurred at the Neustadt site in January 2025 (2 injured) and temporarily disrupting operations; the company’s 2025 environmental report confirms continued operation of the two-site complex
Strategic role: Bavaria’s largest refining company and an important inland fuel supplier for southern Germany and Austria
Risks: Pipeline-supply disruption (full dependance on Trieste/TAL), industrial fires and unit outages, high European energy and carbon costs, declining regional fuel demand and Rhine/Alpine logistics constraints</description>
