		<Placemark id="3C25956D108FB1189A11">
			<name>Naftan Oil Refinery</name>
			<description>Refinery: Naftan Oil Refinery
Classification: Large refinery — not a mega-refinery
Location: Novopolotsk (Navapolatsk), Vitebsk Region, northern Belarus, on the Western Dvina River. Coordinates are an approximate placement on the refinery complex on the city’s southern side; not independently verified against a numbered survey source.
Owner: Belarusian state (99.83%), via the Belneftekhim concern
Capacity: Approximately 12 million tonnes per year primary processing (roughly 240,000 barrels per day); a delayed-coking complex commissioned in 2022 lifted processing depth to about 97.5%
Main feedstocks: Russian crude delivered via the northern branch of the Druzhba pipeline
Main products: Diesel, gasoline, fuel oil, LPG, bitumen, sulfur and petrochemical intermediates
Markets: Domestic Belarus, with historical exports to Russia, Ukraine, the Baltic states, the Netherlands and the UK, though most Western outlets have closed since 2021–2022 sanctions
Recent data: Added to EU, US, UK, Swiss, Canadian and Ukrainian sanctions lists in 2021–2022; the LLK-Naftan joint venture was renamed/restructured (to “EddyTek”) to work around US sanctions; roughly $1.6 billion invested in modernization as of 2021
Strategic role: One of Belarus’s two major refineries (with Mozyr), critical to national fuel supply and a continuing outlet for Russian crude
Risks: Sanctions, loss of Western export markets and technology access, feedstock dependence on Russia via Druzhba, and workforce instability following mass firings after the 2020 political unrest</description>
