		<Placemark id="C1307EEFEAE7C33C308B">
			<name>Kuibyshev Refinery (Rosneft)</name>
			<description>Refinery: Kuibyshev Refinery (Rosneft)
Classification: Conventional refinery — not a mega-refinery
Location: Groznenskaya Street 25, Samara, Samara Oblast, Russia
Owner: Rosneft, via JSC Kuibyshev Refinery
Capacity: About 7 million tonnes per year primary processing, equivalent to roughly 140,000 barrels per day; part of Rosneft’s three-refinery Samara hub alongside Novokuibyshevsk and Syzran
Main feedstocks: Crude from Western Siberia and the Samara region
Main products: Euro-5 gasoline and diesel, aviation kerosene, bitumen, LPG
Markets: Volga region and Russia’s domestic market
Recent data: A drone strike on 10 June 2026 hit both primary crude distillation units (CDU-4 and CDU-5, each around 73,000 barrels per day), forcing a full shutdown and starting fires; sister plants Syzran and Novokuibyshevsk have also been struck in the same campaign
Strategic role: One of three Rosneft refineries in the Samara hub, a major Volga-region fuel supplier established in 1945
Risks: Drone attacks, prolonged unit outages, sanctions, difficulty sourcing replacement equipment and catalysts, and fires</description>
