		<Placemark id="09F771CFD83F3A0A2DFF">
			<name>Aqaba storage</name>
			<description>Terminal: Aqaba oil terminal &amp; storage
Classification: Jordan&apos;s sole maritime energy gateway
Location: Gulf of Aqaba, south of Aqaba city, Jordan
Owner/Operator: Jordanian state port entities (Aqaba Development Corporation area); serves national fuel imports
Handles: Crude and refined-product imports for the Jordanian market, LPG, and LNG via a floating import terminal berth
Connectivity: Crude and products move onward largely by road toward the Zarqa refinery region and inland demand centres
Strategic role: Virtually all of Jordan&apos;s hydrocarbon imports enter through this short stretch of coast — the country&apos;s single energy artery
Risks: Same Bab el-Mandeb exposure as neighbouring Eilat (freight and insurance costs spiked during the Red Sea crisis); single-gateway dependence; limited storage depth</description>
