		</Placemark>
		<Placemark>
			<name>Strasbourg oil terminal</name>
			<description>Terminal: Port aux Pétroles de Strasbourg — Rhine fuel depot cluster
Classification: Inland refined-products storage and distribution hub — France&apos;s second river port
Location: La Robertsau, Port of Strasbourg, Alsace, France — on the Rhine
Owner/Operator: Cluster of seven Seveso high-threshold sites operated by independent storage and distribution companies (including Bolloré Energy and Tepsa) within the Port Autonome de Strasbourg
Infrastructure: Dedicated oil basin (opened in the 1920s, rebuilt after WWII) with barge unloading berths and product tank farms; rail and truck loading
Handles: Diesel, gasoline, heating oil, jet fuel and chemical products — no crude
Connectivity: Supplied mainly by barge from the ARA hub via the Rhine (through the Kaub chokepoint); distributes fuel to service stations across Alsace and eastern France
Recent data: Directly exposed to the August 2026 record low water on the Rhine — reduced barge loads and a ~400% surge in Rotterdam–south Germany product freight tighten and reprice inland supply
Strategic role: The end-point of the ARA-to-Alsace product chain — where a Rhine low-water event becomes a local fuel-supply and price issue
Risks: Rhine navigability (recurring droughts 2018, 2022, 2026); Seveso sites 100 m from housing (contested technological-risk plan); limited pipeline alternatives for the region</description>
			<LookAt>
				<longitude>7.810384275813795</longitude>
				<latitude>48.59896112534291</latitude>
				<altitude>0</altitude>
				<heading>0.03761259590973835</heading>
				<tilt>12.33929695322486</tilt>
				<range>3728.000555799524</range>
