		<Placemark id="07C24C13813F39F143AC">
			<name>Tawke oil field</name>
			<description>Operational status: Uncertain/volatile — as of the last confirmed report (March 13, 2026), DNO had shut down production as a precaution amid the Iran-Israel-US war (following earlier damaging drone strikes in July 2025); I found no more recent confirmation of whether production has resumed since then
Role: Onshore field complex (Tawke + Peshkabir), Kurdistan Region, Iraq; includes a gas-capture/reinjection project cutting Peshkabir&apos;s emissions intensity roughly in half
Operator: DNO ASA 75% (operator); Genel Energy 25%
Capacity: 2025 average gross production ~70,100 boe/d, rising to ~77,300 boe/d by Q4 2025 after maintenance; target of 100,000 boe/d from Tawke+Peshkabir combined; historical run-rate had been over 100,000–120,000 bopd in 2019–2020
Recent data: Production resumed/ramped in Feb 2026 after a 30-month drilling hiatus tied to the 2023–2025 KRG export-pipeline closure, backed by a two-rig (soon three-rig), eight-well 2026 drilling program and $100 million planned Kurdistan capex (vs. $22 million in 2025) — before the March 2026 war-related shutdown described above; license runs to 2026 with an automatic 5-year extension option to 2031 (potentially to 2036)
Risks: Direct exposure to the 2025–26 regional war (drone strikes, precautionary shutdowns); recurring KRG–Baghdad export-pipeline disputes/closures; Kurdistan political and security risk generally; execution risk on the newly restarted drilling campaign</description>
