		<Placemark id="00FD4B720E3F39F9EB09">
			<name>Shaikan oil filed</name>
			<description>Operational status: Currently suspended (as of late July 2026) — precautionary shutdown amid Iran-Israel-US conflict spillover into the region; this is the field&apos;s second shut-in this year (also halted briefly in Feb 2026).
Role: Onshore oil field ~60 km northwest of Erbil, Kurdistan Region, northern Iraq; producing since 2013.
Operator: Gulf Keystone Petroleum (80% working interest, operator); MOL Group holds the remaining 20%.
Capacity: Two production facilities, ~60,000 bopd total processing capacity; gross 2P reserves of 416 million bbl (as of Dec 2025), ~27 years of reserve life at current rates.
Recent data: Averaged ~41,560 bopd in 2025 (briefly exceeded 45,000 bopd just before the July suspension); cumulative production over 150 million bbl since 2013; ~$269m revenue on 9.6 million bbl produced in the first 8 months of 2025.
Risks: Sole export route is the Iraq-Turkey (Ceyhan) pipeline system with no redundancy; recurring shutdowns tied to Iran-related regional conflict; unresolved Baghdad-Erbil payment disputes; scheduled US troop withdrawal from Kurdistan by Sept 30, 2026 removes an implicit security backstop.</description>
