		<Placemark id="0C734745E640214C7E68">
			<name>Tengiz, Drilling oil filed (CPC blend)</name>
			<description>Operational status: Operational — recovered from a major January 2026 power-facility fire that forced a near-total shutdown for most of that month; full production (~950,000 bopd) was targeted for restoration by Feb 23, 2026, and no further disruption reports found since
Role: Kazakhstan&apos;s largest oil field, onshore near the Caspian Sea; crude blended into &quot;CPC Blend&quot; and exported via the Caspian Pipeline Consortium (CPC) pipeline to the Black Sea (Novorossiysk)
Operator: Tengizchevroil (TCO) — Chevron 50% (operator), ExxonMobil 25%, KazMunayGas 20%, LukArco 5%; JV formed 1993 under a 40-year development agreement
Capacity: ~950,000 bopd (~120,000 tonnes/day) following completion of the Future Growth Project–Wellhead Pressure Management Project (FGP-WPMP) expansion (WPMP started April 2024; FGP first oil January 2025) — roughly 50% higher than pre-expansion output
Recent data: January 2026 fires at onsite power facilities forced a near-complete shutdown; CPC loadings</description>
