		<Placemark>
			<name>Dalia oil field</name>
			<description>Operational status: Operational — producing since 2006, now in decline as a mature deepwater field
Role: Deepwater FPSO field, Block 17, offshore Angola, ~4,116 ft (1,255 m) water depth; one of four FPSOs on Block 17 alongside Girassol, Pazflor and CLOV
Operator: TotalEnergies (Total E&amp;P Angola); partners include Equinor, ExxonMobil, Azule Energy (BP/Eni JV) and Sonangol — same consortium structure as Girassol (TotalEnergies 38%, Equinor 22%, ExxonMobil 19%, Azule 15%, Sonangol 5%)
Capacity: Peaked around 240,000 bopd (2010); ~487 million barrels of remaining recoverable reserves (68% already recovered); production guided to continue to an economic limit around 2046
Recent data: Block 17 output is declining from peak levels overall; TotalEnergies is offsetting this with the Begonia subsea tieback (~30,000 bopd) and a CLOV Phase 3 infill project to extend plateau production — both block-wide rather than Dalia-specific boosts
Risks: Natural decline from a maturing 20-year-old field; standard deepwater operational and spill risk; reliance on subsea tiebacks/infill drilling rather than new discoveries to sustain block output</description>
