		<Placemark>
			<name>Gialo Oil Field</name>
			<description>Operational status: Operational — producing since 1961, still active as of 2026
Role: Onshore field, Sirte Basin, Libya (28.71°N, 21.38°E); one of the original Waha concession fields, linked to Es Sider export terminal via the Gialo-Waha pipeline
Operator: Waha Oil Company (NOC/ConocoPhillips/TotalEnergies JV — same ownership as the wider Waha concessions: NOC 59.16%, ConocoPhillips 20.42%, TotalEnergies 20.42%)
Capacity: ~130,000 bopd design capacity (2020); actual output has run well above that historically (~245,000 bopd in 2012) and likely below it more recently as the field matures
Recent data: Adjacent North Gialo field (separate, in-development, FID 2019) is the ~100,000 boe/d expansion project tied to Waha&apos;s January 2026 concession-extension deal — not part of Gialo&apos;s own output, but directly next to it
Risks: Libya&apos;s recurring political fragmentation and force-majeure/blockade risk (resurfaced as recently as May 2025); mature-field natural decline; shared exposure with the wider Waha system to national oil-sector disruption</description>
			<Camera>
				<longitude>21.41730238096121</longitude>
				<latitude>28.67981021896902</latitude>
				<altitude>14707.00906128159</altitude>
