		<Placemark>
			<name>Waha Oil Field</name>
			<description>Operational status: Operational — ~370,000 boe/d across the Waha concessions as of January 2026
Role: Onshore oil field/concession complex, Sirte Basin, Libya (28.74°N, 21.44°E); producing since 1963; feeds the Es Sider export terminal
Operator: Waha Oil Company — JV of NOC (Libya) 59.16%, ConocoPhillips 20.42%, TotalEnergies 20.42%
Capacity: ~370,000 boe/d currently; ~630 million barrels remaining oil reserves (2020); North Gialo field development could add another ~100,000 boe/d
Recent data: Concessions extended to December 2050 via a January 2026 agreement with revised fiscal terms meant to boost output; 7 exploration wells and seismic work planned for 2026
Risks: Libya&apos;s recurring political fragmentation between rival governments, with force-majeure/blockade risk resurfacing as recently as May 2025; historical precedent of eastern-faction oil blockades sharply cutting national output; standard mature-field decline risk</description>
